NAME
     od - dump a file in octal, hexadecimal or characters

SYNOPSIS
     od [-bcdosvx] [-A a|d|o|x|n] [-j SKIP] [-N COUNT] [FILE...]
     hexdump [-C] [FILE...]
     xxd [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
     od prints the bytes of each FILE in the form the options ask for.
     Called as hexdump or xxd it starts from the conventions of those
     commands instead: hexdump -C is the usual hexadecimal-and-text
     dump.

OPTIONS
     -b   bytes in octal
     -c   bytes as characters, with escapes
     -d   two-byte decimal
     -o   two-byte octal
     -s   two-byte signed decimal
     -x   two-byte hexadecimal
     -A X   how to print the offsets: octal, decimal, hex, or none
     -j SKIP    start SKIP bytes in
     -N COUNT   stop after COUNT bytes
     -v   do not fold repeated lines into a star

SEE ALSO
     strings(1), file(1), dd(1)
